2026-11-12T03:36:34.2940906Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3036903Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3045641Z [0m
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3046622Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3047475Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3048090Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3048765Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3050006Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3050787Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3051823Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3053186Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3053485Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3054143Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3054981Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3055766Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3056373Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3056651Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3056940Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3057396Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3057817Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3058254Z    can use Nix.
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3058426Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3058597Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3058769Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3059468Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3060026Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3060281Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3060400Z I will:
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3060648Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3060838Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3061338Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3061795Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3062225Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3062600Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3062927Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3063391Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3063905Z    /root
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3072974Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3073806Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3082960Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3083633Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3083906Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3084703Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3085219Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3101899Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3102844Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3111783Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3112720Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3113386Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3113674Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3114001Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3114423Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3114944Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3115746Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3116162Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3116340Z If you would like to
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3116729Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3116979Z 
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3117222Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3117694Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-12T03:36:34.3117855Z 
